k</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="sk">Zvitok</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="pl">Zwój</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="da">Skriftrulle</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="ca">Rotlle</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="nl">Boekrol</skos:prefLabel><skos:note xml:lang="de">Handschrift in Rollenform (Vorläufer des Kodex und des Buches)</skos:note><skos:note xml:lang="fi">Rullalle kääritty teksti</skos:note><skos:note xml:lang="en">Roll of papyrus, parchment, or paper containing writing</skos:note><skos:note xml:lang="fr">Support d'écriture sous la forme d'un rouleau de papyrus ou de parchemin</skos:note><skos:note xml:lang="es">Lámina, generalmente de papiro o pergamino enrollada sobre sí misma, en que se escribía</skos:note><skos:broader rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/concept/17"/><skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q720106"/><skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="https://d-nb.info/gnd/4146829-6"/><skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="https://www.freebase.com/m/047rtk"/><skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="https://g.co/kg/m/047rtk"/><skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300028629"/><skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://iconclass.org/49L71"/><skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Scroll"/></skos:Concept><ore:Aggregation rdf:about="http://data.europeana.eu/aggregation/provider/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_cb_0603"><edm:aggregatedCHO rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/item/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_cb_0603"/><edm:dataProvider rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/organization/1482250000004502183"></edm:dataProvider><edm:isShownAt rdf:resource="http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/list/one/fmb/cb-0603"/><edm:isShownBy rdf:resource="http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/loris/fmb/fmb-cb-0603/fmb-cb-0603_e011.jp2/full/full/0/default.jpg"/><edm:object rdf:resource="http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/loris/fmb/fmb-cb-0603/fmb-cb-0603_e011.jp2/full/full/0/default.jpg"/><edm:provider rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/organization/1482250000004671163"></edm:provider><edm:rights rdf:resource="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/3.0/"/></ore:Aggregation><ore:Proxy rdf:about="http://data.europeana.eu/proxy/europeana/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_cb_0603"><dc:type rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/concept/2849"></dc:type><dcterms:medium rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/concept/2090"></dcterms:medium><edm:europeanaProxy>true</edm:europeanaProxy><ore:proxyFor rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/item/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_cb_0603"/><ore:proxyIn rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/aggregation/europeana/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_cb_0603"/><edm:type>TEXT</edm:type></ore:Proxy><ore:Proxy rdf:about="http://data.europeana.eu/proxy/provider/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_cb_0603"><dc:creator>Xuanzang</dc:creator><dc:date>very likely 12th century</dc:date><dc:description>The handscroll of Daihannya-haramitta-kyō, the Sutra of Great Wisdom, chapter five hundred and forty, consists of a simple sheet of paper without mounting. The complete version of the sutra encompasses six-hundred chapters. It was introduced to China from India by the monk, scholar and translator Xuanzang, who translated the sutra into Chinese in the 7th century before it was imported into Japan. The sutra is written in black ink on high-quality paper, very likely kōzo-shi, which is made using the fibre of Broussonetia papyrifera or paper mulberry tree, especially treasured and used for important documents during the early periods of Japanese history such as the Nara and Heian periods. There is a circular red seal placed over the top of the first four lines of the text, stating “Yakushi-ji-in” (seal of the temple Yakushi-ji). The sutra was written in Japan within the context of the religious rites of reproducing holy scripture to benefit the karma.</dc:description><dc:format>1 f., 23.6 x 883 cm</dc:format><dc:identifier>doi:10.5076/e-codices-fmb-cb-0603</dc:identifier><dc:identifier>http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/list/one/fmb/cb-0603</dc:identifier><dc:identifier>Cologny, Fondation Martin Bodmer, Cod. Bodmer 603</dc:identifier><dc:publisher>e-codices - Virtual Manuscript Library of Switzerland</dc:publisher><dc:language>Chinese</dc:language><dc:rights>e-codices / Cologny, Fondation Martin Bodmer (cf. http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/about/terms)</dc:rights><dc:source rdf:resource="http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/list/one/fmb/cb-0603"></dc:source><dc:title>Cologny, Fondation Martin Bodmer, Cod. Bodmer 603 : Daihannya-haramitta-kyō, kan gohyaku-yonjū (Sutra of Great Wisdom Chapter 540)</dc:title><dc:type>Scroll</dc:type><dcterms:medium>Paper</dcterms:medium><edm:europeanaProxy>false</edm:europeanaProxy><ore:proxyFor rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/item/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_cb_0603"/><ore:proxyIn rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/aggregation/provider/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_cb_0603"/><edm:type>TEXT</edm:type></ore:Proxy><edm:EuropeanaAggregation rdf:about="http://data.europeana.eu/aggregation/europeana/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_cb_0603"><edm:aggregatedCHO rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/item/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_cb_0603"/><edm:datasetName>9200211_Ag_EU_e-Codices</edm:datasetName><edm:country>Switzerland</edm:country><edm:preview rdf:resource="http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/loris/fmb/fmb-cb-0603/fmb-cb-0603_e011.jp2/full/full/0/default.jpg"/><edm:landingPage rdf:resource="https://www.europeana.eu/item/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_cb_0603"/><edm:language>mul</edm:language><edm:rights rdf:resource="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/3.0/"/><edm:completeness>10</edm:completeness><dcterms:created>2016-09-09T12:30:00.195Z</dcterms:created><dcterms:modified>2016-09-27T09:30:13.203Z</dcterms:modified><dqv:hasQualityAnnotation rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/item/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_cb_0603#contentTier"/><dqv:hasQualityAnnotation rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/item/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_cb_0603#metadataTier"/></edm:EuropeanaA